{"id":47099036064691,"type":"album","name":"Faith in Strangers","artist":"Andy Stott","year":2014,"weight":13,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/2014/20712-faith-in-strangers.jpg","aoty":81,"aoty_user":78,"yt":"7Hp2F29zktk","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/andy-stott/faith-in-strangers","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/20712-andy-stott-faith-in-strangers.php"},"desc":"Faith In Strangers’ was written and produced between January 2013 and June 2014, and was edited and sequenced in late July this year. Making use of on an array of instruments, field recordings, found sounds and vocal treatments, it’s a largely analogue variant of hi-tech production styles arcing from the dissonant to the sublime. The first two tracks recorded during these early sessions bookend the release, the opener ‘Time Away’ featuring Euphonium played by Kim Holly Thorpe and last track ‘Missing’ a contribution by Stott’s occasional vocal collaborator Alison Skidmore who also appeared on 2012’s ‘Luxury Problems’. Between these two ."},"artist_ref":{"id":177852440425109,"name":"Andy Stott","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Andy_stott_cmky_2009.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":65067151178508,"type":"genre","name":"Electronic Dance Music","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":244,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":15318882910861,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":224,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":129140599487979,"type":"genre","name":"Deconstructed Club","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":207,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":15772809314424,"type":"genre","name":"UK Bass","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":201,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":279372668204783,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — UK Bass","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":6,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":97390058649005,"name":"RYM Top — Elect